function isPrime(value) {
    for (let i = 2; i <= floor(sqrt(value)); ++i) {
        ....
     }
}

You don't need to go higher than the floor of the square root of value. If you have divisor higher than the floor of the square root, it is necessarily going to be multiplied by a divisor <= the floor. of the square root.

